You're absolutely right, and I apologize for not looking more carefully. Let me trace the actual issue.

The problem is in your HTML structure - you have nested map-container divs with the map controls inside a duplicate structure. Look at this section in your Dashboard tab:

```html
<div class="map-container" role="region" aria-label="Interactive site map">
    <div id="map"></div>
    
<div class="map-container" role="region" aria-label="Interactive site map">
    <div id="map"></div>
    <!-- Add this fallback message -->
    <div id="mapFallback" style="display: none; text-align: center; padding: 20px;">
        <i class="bi bi-map"></i>
        <p>Map is loading. Please wait...</p>
    </div>

    <div class="map-controls" ...>
        ...
    </div>
```

The first </div> after <div id="map"></div> closes the first map-container prematurely, leaving the second map-container open. This creates invalid HTML and confuses Leaflet.

The Fix - Replace the entire map section in your Dashboard tab (around line 845-920) with this:

```html
<div class="map-container" role="region" aria-label="Interactive site map">
    <div id="map"></div>
    <div id="mapFallback" style="display: none; text-align: center; padding: 20px;">
        <i class="bi bi-map"></i>
        <p>Map is loading. Please wait...</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="map-controls" role="group" aria-label="Map controls">
        <div class="btn-group-vertical w-100">
            <div class="btn-group">
                <button id="zoneToggle" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary active" 
                        aria-pressed="true" aria-label="Toggle zones layer">
                    Zones
                </button>
                <button id="vegetationToggle" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" 
                        aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Toggle vegetation layer">
                    Vegetation
                </button>
                <button id="weedsToggle" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger" 
                        aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Toggle weeds layer">
                    Weeds
                </button>
            </div>
            <hr class="my-1">
            <div class="btn-group">
                <button id="editModeBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-warning" 
                        aria-label="Toggle edit mode">
                    <i class="bi bi-pencil-square"></i> Edit Mode
                </button>
                <button id="saveMapBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-success" 
                        aria-label="Save map changes">
                    <i class="bi bi-save"></i> Save
                </button>
                <button id="clearMapBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-danger" 
                        aria-label="Clear all drawings">
                    <i class="bi bi-trash"></i> Clear
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="map-legend" id="mapLegend">
        <div class="map-legend-item">
            <div class="map-legend-color" style="background: #3498db80;"></div>
            <span>Zones</span>
        </div>
        <div class="map-legend-item">
            <div class="map-legend-color" style="background: #27ae60;"></div>
            <span>Vegetation</span>
        </div>
        <div class="map-legend-item">
            <div class="map-legend-color" style="background: #e74c3c;"></div>
            <span>Weeds</span>
        </div>
        <div class="map-legend-item">
            <div class="marker-color-sample" style="background: #f1c40f;"></div>
            <span>Pins</span>
        </div>
        <div class="map-legend-item">
            <div class="marker-color-sample" style="background: #9b59b6;"></div>
            <span>Points of Interest</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
```

The key change: One single map-container div containing all elements, not nested duplicates.
